{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","text":"AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","text":"Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}]}]},{"name":"clock","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock that measures the gaps."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tolerance of the timer’s sleeps. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws, without waiting for the upstream to respond to the cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Example","level":2,"anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["let clock = ContinuousClock()","for try await line in bytes.lines.timeout(.seconds(30), clock: clock) {","    handle(line)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"TimeoutError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"customError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuspendingClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the given clock."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOnCastAfterFlatMapping\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/retryoncastafterflatmapping\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customerror:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","modules":[{"name":"Afluent","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"iPadOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"Mac Catalyst","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"macOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","name":"tvOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","name":"watchOS","beta":false}],"role":"symbol","title":"timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE7timeout_5clock9tolerance11customErrorAA14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutVy_xqd__G8DurationQyd___qd__AOSgs0H0_pSgt12_Concurrency5ClockRd__lF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO27RetryOnCastAfterFlatMappingC","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","t